      <author>eurodrigolira@gmail.com (Rodrigo Lira)</author>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/oracle-vm-server-anti-affinity-group/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://rodrigolira.eti.br/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/oracle_vm.gif&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer&#34;&gt;&lt;figure&gt;&lt;img&#xA;    class=&#34;my-0 rounded-md&#34;&#xA;    loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;    decoding=&#34;async&#34;&#xA;    fetchpriority=&#34;auto&#34;&#xA;    alt=&#34;&#34;&#xA;    width=&#34;200&#34;&#xA;    height=&#34;98&#34;&#xA;    src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/oracle-vm-server-anti-affinity-group/images/oracle_vm.gif&#34;&#xA;    srcset=&#34;http://localhost:1313/oracle-vm-server-anti-affinity-group/images/oracle_vm.gif 800w, http://localhost:1313/oracle-vm-server-anti-affinity-group/images/oracle_vm.gif 1280w&#34;&#xA;    sizes=&#34;(min-width: 768px) 50vw, 65vw&#34;&#xA;    data-zoom-src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/oracle-vm-server-anti-affinity-group/images/oracle_vm.gif&#34;&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Salve Salve Pessoal!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;O anti-affinity group ou grupo anti-afinidade especifica que máquinas virtuais nunca devem ser executadas no mesmo servidor Oracle VM. Um grupo anti-afinidade aplica-se a todos os servidores em um pool de servidores.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
